import BlueprintPage from '../components/BlueprintPage.astro'; const sections=[{title:'Start with your learning goals',paragraphs:['Students can share their course, year, syllabus, interests, and practical requirements through the existing enquiry route. Availability must be confirmed directly.','A useful enquiry is specific without sharing patient information. Include your university or training institution, programme and year, dates or duration required by your course, learning areas you hope to explore, and any required documentation. Mention whether your institution requires a named supervisor, attendance records, a formal letter, or a final evaluation. These details help the team understand your request but do not guarantee a placement.','Before accepting an opportunity, ask who would supervise learning, what activities are permitted, how often supervision occurs, what hours are expected, and whether the placement matches your institution’s requirements. Confirm fees, schedule, attendance, location and documentation directly. Do not assume a certificate, caseload, clinical access or placement length unless explicitly agreed.']},{title:'Ethical boundaries',paragraphs:['Clinical exposure must respect patient choice, confidentiality, supervision, and scope. Students do not independently diagnose or provide therapy.','Patient privacy takes priority over observation or coursework. Do not record, photograph, copy, or discuss identifiable clinical information outside an explicitly approved and supervised process. A patient’s choice about student presence must be respected without pressure. Students should not offer advice, promise outcomes, interpret tests independently, or represent themselves as clinicians. Questions should go to the assigned supervisor.','A responsible learning experience makes boundaries clear before activities begin. Ask how consent is handled, what to do if a patient declines observation, where questions can be raised, and how concerns are escalated. If a task falls outside your training or supervision, pause and seek guidance. These safeguards protect patients and help students understand professional practice.']},{title:'What a placement can and cannot promise',paragraphs:['An enquiry is a request for information, not confirmation of a position. The clinic may need to review availability, learning goals, supervision capacity and fit with university requirements before responding. Do not make travel or academic plans until dates and expectations are confirmed.','A placement cannot replace formal coursework, licensure requirements, or supervision arranged by your university. Observation or participation depends on patient consent, clinical appropriateness, and the supervising professional. Students remain responsible for confirming that the experience satisfies their institution’s rules.']},{title:'How to make an enquiry',paragraphs:['Use the training enquiry route linked on this page and give a reliable way to reply. A concise message can state your programme and year, institution, required duration or hours, date range, learning goals and any supervision or documentation requirements. The clinic can then explain whether a suitable opportunity may be available and what its terms are.','If your course requires a specific format, attach only the relevant blank form or requirement. Do not send patient details, academic passwords, identity documents that have not been requested, or sensitive health information. For general clinic questions, use the contact page.']},{title:'A respectful approach to clinical learning',paragraphs:['Psychology training involves careful listening, evidence-informed thinking, humility and respect for people’s lived experience. Students can prepare by reviewing ethics, asking clear questions, arriving on time and keeping learning notes free of identifying details. It is appropriate to say when you do not know something and seek supervision rather than guessing.','Patient services and academic enquiries have separate purposes. To understand clinical roles, see the doctors and services pages; to ask about a training opportunity, use the dedicated enquiry form. No clinical appointment or patient service is included by virtue of an academic enquiry.']}];
